{"byteLength":625,"contentHash":{"algorithm":"sha256","value":"feb898c94697b81ae9b146320909638c27def892020f7ac3ae988e186913f67b"},"kind":"skillDocument","name":"references/stdlib/RoundingMode.md","producer":{"build":{"commit":"5de2594ad523fba4f38fa63f7a1b306e8a23eb0c","dirty":false,"provenance":{"commit":"git","dirty":"environment"},"target":"aarch64-apple-darwin"},"name":"benitoite","version":"0.0.13"},"schemaVersion":1,"text":"# Benitoite.RoundingMode\n\nStatus: standard, in the prelude. It can be used without `import`.\n\nRefer to its declarations as `RoundingMode.<name>`, for example `RoundingMode.RoundingMode`.\n\nRounding directions for `Decimal.round`.\n\n```benitoite\npublic data RoundingMode\n  /// The nearest value; halves go to the value whose last digit is even.\n  HalfToEven\n  /// The nearest value; halves go away from zero.\n  HalfAwayFromZero\n  /// Toward zero.\n  TowardZero\n  /// Toward negative infinity.\n  TowardNegativeInfinity\n  /// Toward positive infinity.\n  TowardPositiveInfinity\nend data\n```\n\nHow `Decimal.round` chooses the result.\n"}
